# Essay 7 — Communication

## Question

Modern technology has made communication faster and easier, but it has reduced the quality of personal relationships. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Modern technology has made it much easier for people to communicate with one another. However, some people believe that it has harmed the quality of personal relationships. I partly agree with this view because technology can reduce face-to-face communication, although it also helps people maintain relationships over long distances.

On the one hand, technology can have a negative effect on personal relationships. Many people now prefer sending text messages or using social media instead of meeting their friends and relatives in person. As a result, conversations may become shorter and less meaningful. For example, family members may sit together in the same room while using their phones rather than talking to each other. This can gradually create emotional distance between them.

On the other hand, modern technology has made it easier to maintain relationships when people live far apart. Video calls, instant messaging and social media allow people to communicate regularly without travelling long distances. For instance, a person who works abroad can easily speak to their parents through a video call. Therefore, technology can actually strengthen relationships when it is used properly.

In conclusion, I partly agree that technology has reduced the quality of some personal relationships because it can replace face-to-face interaction. Nevertheless, it is also a valuable tool for keeping people connected, particularly when they live far away from each other.

