# Essay 24 — Examinations

## Question

Examinations are the best way to measure a student's academic performance. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Some people argue that examinations are the best method of measuring students' academic performance. I disagree with this view because exams can measure knowledge effectively, but they do not always show a student's full range of abilities.

Examinations have some important advantages. They provide a standard method of assessing a large number of students. In addition, students are often required to study a wide range of subjects before an examination. This can encourage them to develop knowledge and prepare seriously for their courses. For example, a final examination can show whether a student understands the main concepts taught during a semester.

However, exams cannot measure every important skill. Some students perform poorly under pressure even though they understand the subject well. Moreover, abilities such as creativity, teamwork, communication and practical skills are difficult to assess through a written examination. Projects, presentations and classroom activities can provide a more complete picture of a student's performance.

In conclusion, I do not agree that examinations are the best way to measure academic performance. They are useful for testing knowledge, but a combination of exams, projects and practical assessments would provide a fairer evaluation of students.

