# Essay 29 — Celebrities as Role Models

## Question

Celebrities have a responsibility to act as good role models for young people. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Some people believe that celebrities have a responsibility to set a good example for young people. I largely agree because celebrities have a strong influence on their followers, although parents and schools also have an important role in guiding children.

Celebrities can influence young people's behaviour because they are widely followed on television and social media. Young people may copy their clothing, language, lifestyle and even their attitudes. Therefore, celebrities should think carefully about their public behaviour. For example, a famous athlete who promotes discipline and a healthy lifestyle can encourage young fans to exercise and work hard.

However, celebrities cannot be fully responsible for the behaviour of young people. Parents should teach children the difference between good and bad behaviour, while schools should provide moral and social education. In addition, young people should gradually learn to make their own decisions instead of copying everything they see online.

In conclusion, I agree that celebrities should behave responsibly because they can strongly influence young people. Nevertheless, parents, teachers and young people themselves also share responsibility for developing positive behaviour.

