# Essay 32 — Television and Children

## Question

Watching television is a waste of time for children. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Some people believe that watching television is a waste of time for children. I partly disagree because excessive television viewing can be harmful, but educational and age-appropriate programmes can also benefit children.

On the one hand, watching too much television can have several negative effects. Children who spend many hours in front of a screen may have less time for exercise, reading and social activities. It can also affect their concentration and sleep if they watch television late at night. For example, a child who spends most of the afternoon watching entertainment programmes may have less time to complete homework or play outdoors.

On the other hand, television can be educational when children watch suitable programmes. Documentaries and educational shows can teach them about science, history, nature and different cultures. Furthermore, some programmes can help children develop their vocabulary and general knowledge.

In conclusion, I do not completely agree that television is a waste of time for children. The main issue is not television itself but how much children watch and what type of programmes they choose. Parents should therefore control their children's screen time and encourage educational content.

