# Essay 35 — Plastic Pollution

## Question

Plastic pollution is the most serious environmental problem facing the world today. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Plastic pollution has become a major environmental problem, and some people consider it the most serious issue facing the world today. I partly agree because plastic causes widespread damage, but climate change and other environmental problems are also extremely serious.

Plastic pollution is particularly harmful because plastic products can remain in the environment for many years. Large amounts of plastic waste enter rivers and oceans, where they can harm animals and damage ecosystems. In addition, tiny pieces of plastic can enter the food chain. For example, sea animals may eat plastic waste because they mistake it for food.

However, other environmental problems should not be ignored. Climate change can lead to rising temperatures, extreme weather and sea-level rise, affecting millions of people. Deforestation is another serious issue because forests absorb carbon dioxide and provide homes for many species. Therefore, it is difficult to say that plastic pollution is more serious than every other environmental problem.

In conclusion, I agree that plastic pollution is one of the world's most serious environmental challenges, but I would not consider it the single greatest problem. Governments should tackle plastic waste while also taking strong action against climate change and deforestation.

