# Essay 39 — Elderly People and Retirement Homes

## Question

Elderly people should live with their family members rather than in retirement homes. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Some people believe that elderly people should live with their families instead of living in retirement homes. I partly agree because living with relatives can provide emotional support, but professional care may be more suitable for some elderly people.

Living with family members can have several benefits. Older people may feel less lonely when they live with their children and grandchildren. They can also maintain close family relationships and receive daily support. For example, family members can help an elderly person with shopping, cooking and other household activities. This can make older people feel valued and respected.

However, retirement homes can provide professional care that some families cannot offer. Elderly people with serious physical problems may need trained nurses and medical assistance. In addition, their family members may have full-time jobs and may not have enough time to provide constant care. A good retirement home can also offer social activities and opportunities for elderly residents to interact with people of a similar age.

In conclusion, I believe that living with family is beneficial for many elderly people, but retirement homes can be a better choice when professional care is required. The decision should depend on the person's health, preferences and family circumstances.

