# Essay 45 — Parents and Childcare

## Question

Both parents should share equal responsibility for childcare and housework. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Some people believe that both parents should share equal responsibility for childcare and housework. I strongly agree because this arrangement is fairer and can create a healthier family environment.

Firstly, sharing household responsibilities can reduce the pressure on one parent. In many families, both parents now work outside the home, so it is unreasonable for one person to be responsible for most household tasks. If both parents contribute, they can manage their time more effectively and have less stress. For example, one parent can prepare meals while the other takes care of the children.

Secondly, equal participation can teach children important values. Children can learn that household responsibilities should be shared rather than being the duty of one particular gender. They may also develop greater respect for both parents when they see them working together. In addition, parents can spend more quality time with their children when childcare is shared.

In conclusion, I strongly agree that both parents should share responsibility for childcare and housework. This can reduce stress, promote equality and create a more supportive family environment.

