# Essay 55 — Refugees from War-Torn Countries

## Question

Rich countries should accept more refugees from war-torn nations. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Some people argue that wealthy countries should accept more refugees from countries affected by war. I largely agree because refugees often have no safe place to live, although receiving countries must also consider their resources and social stability.

The main reason for accepting more refugees is humanitarian. People living in war zones may lose their homes, jobs and family members, and they may face serious threats to their lives. Wealthy countries generally have better resources and can provide shelter, education and healthcare. Giving refugees a safe place can therefore protect vulnerable people and help them rebuild their lives.

However, countries cannot accept an unlimited number of refugees without careful planning. A sudden increase in population can place pressure on housing, schools and healthcare systems. Governments should therefore establish a controlled system and ensure that refugees can integrate into society. For example, language classes and employment programmes can help newcomers become independent and contribute to the economy.

In conclusion, I agree that wealthy countries should accept more refugees from war-torn nations because they have greater resources and a humanitarian responsibility. Nevertheless, refugee programmes should be properly planned so that both refugees and host communities can benefit.

