# Essay 58 — Tourism and Local Communities

## Question

Tourism has more negative impacts than positive effects on local communities. To what extent do you agree or disagree?

## Sample Answer

Tourism can bring significant economic benefits to local communities, but it can also create social and environmental problems. I partly disagree with the statement because I believe that well-managed tourism generally provides more benefits than disadvantages.

One major advantage of tourism is that it creates employment and supports local businesses. Hotels, restaurants, transport services and shops can earn money from visitors. Tourism can also encourage governments to improve roads, public transport and other facilities. For example, a popular tourist destination may attract investment and create new jobs for local residents.

However, tourism can have negative effects when it is poorly managed. A large number of visitors can produce waste, increase traffic and damage natural areas. In addition, popular destinations may become more expensive for local people because demand for housing and other services increases. Traditional areas can also lose some of their original character if they are developed mainly for tourists.

In conclusion, tourism can have both positive and negative effects on local communities. I believe its benefits are greater when governments control tourism carefully and protect the environment and local culture.

