# Final Band 6.5–7 Checklist

Before submitting your essay, check:

- [ ] I clearly answered the question.
- [ ] My opinion is clear in the introduction.
- [ ] My opinion is consistent throughout the essay.
- [ ] I have two well-developed main ideas.
- [ ] I explained each main idea.
- [ ] I gave relevant examples.
- [ ] Every sentence has a subject and a verb.
- [ ] I checked subject–verb agreement.
- [ ] I checked singular and plural nouns.
- [ ] I checked articles: **a / an / the**.
- [ ] I checked verb tenses.
- [ ] I used linking words naturally.
- [ ] I avoided unnecessarily difficult vocabulary.
- [ ] I wrote around **260–290 words**.
- [ ] My conclusion clearly restates my position.

## Key Principle

> **Clear ideas + accurate grammar + logical development + relevant examples + natural vocabulary = Band 6.5–7.**

Do not try to sound extremely sophisticated. A simple sentence that is accurate is much safer than a complicated sentence containing grammatical errors.
